  {
    "index": 3,
    "hash": "TMk7VziuPF5urjcCvFAV+JcnkYA=",
    "timestampUtcMs": "2026-09-03T07:38:05.779Z",
    "action": {
      "type": "SET_CONTENT",
      "input": {
        "content": "`reactor-api` separates GraphQL and HTTP concerns into two independent interfaces so the HTTP framework (currently Express) or the GraphQL engine (currently Apollo) can be replaced without touching application logic.\n\n**`IHttpAdapter`** owns the transport: binding ports, registering routes, and bridging framework-native request/response objects into Fetch API types. `setupMiddleware(config)` installs CORS and body parsing once; `mount(path, handler, opts?)` registers a handler with `exact: false` (default, exact-path match in an internal dispatch map) or `exact: true` (prefix match, router `.use()` semantics); `getRoute` registers read-only GET routes such as `/health` and `/explorer`; `mountRawMiddleware` takes a Connect/Express-compatible function (the Vite dev server) with the cast to the native type **contained inside the adapter**, so call sites need no framework imports; `listen(port, tls?)` returns the `http.Server` so callers can attach WebSocket servers and supports three TLS modes \u2014 `true` (devcert), `{ keyPath, certPath }`, or in-memory `{ cert, key }`. `handle` is a read-only escape hatch to the raw framework object, documented for integrations with no framework-agnostic equivalent yet.\n\n**`IGatewayAdapter<TContext>`** owns GraphQL: `createHandler(schema, contextFactory)` for one subgraph, `createSupergraphHandler(...)` composing all subgraphs via federation, `updateSupergraph()` re-composing the SDL and hot-reloading the running gateway (a no-op before the supergraph handler exists), `attachWebSocket(...)` returning a `WsDisposer`, and `start` / `stop`.\n\nThe contract between them is one type:\n\n```ts\ntype FetchHandler = (request: Request) => Promise<Response>;\n```\n\n\"No Express types cross this boundary.\" That is the whole point \u2014 the gateway produces `FetchHandler`s and the HTTP adapter consumes them.\n\n## Provenance\n- `packages/reactor-api/ARCHITECTURE.md` \u2014 Interfaces (IHttpAdapter, IGatewayAdapter); FetchHandler: the boundary\n- `packages/reactor-api/README.md` \u2014 Core Components \u203a GraphQL Manager (decoupling note)\n\n_Extracted from the Powerhouse repository at **v6.2.2-dev.74**._",
        "updatedAt": "2026-09-03T07:38:05.778Z"
      },
      "timestampUtcMs": "2026-09-03T07:38:05.779Z"
    }
  },
